        "original_id": "770bd71e-f73b-539d-badd-ffb4fdc9884d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: LD Beghtol, Damian Costilla\n- Bands: The Magnetic Fields, Flare Acoustic Arts League, The Smiths, Love, The Velvet Underground\n- Albums and Songs: 69 Love Songs, “The Book of Love”\n- Companies: Merge Records\n- Places: Fort Campbell, Kentucky, New York\n- Topics: experimental pop, indie pop, musical influences\n\nFacts:\n- LD Beghtol was born in 1964 in Fort Campbell, Kentucky, and he is an American musician, art director, and writer.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League, also known as Flare, was formed in New York in 1996 by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was an experimental pop band known for intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was influenced by The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields, Love, various 4AD bands, and The Velvet Underground.\n- LD Beghtol sometimes collaborated with The Magnetic Fields.\n- 69 Love Songs is the sixth studio album by the American indie pop band The Magnetic Fields.\n- 69 Love Songs was released on September 7, 1999, by Merge Records.\n- “The Book of Love” appears on The Magnetic Fields’ three-volume concept album 69 Love Songs.\n- 69 Love Songs contains 69 tracks described as love songs, with 23 tracks in each of its three volumes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
